"""Cybersecurity glossary, part 23: telecom and mobile-money fraud methods, phishing kits, authentication weaknesses, crypto and mobile risks,
vulnerability prioritisation, privacy and breach checking, and how to report. Awareness-level, protective content. fr/rw/sw are a DRAFT for review.
Row layout: see cyber_terms_20.R."""
from cyber_terms_20 import R

TERMS_23 = [
    R("sms-sender-id-spoofing", "SMS sender ID spoofing and SMS gateway abuse", ["sender id spoofing", "sms spoofing", "sms sender spoofing", "spoofed sms", "fake sender name", "alphanumeric sender id", "sms gateway abuse", "bulk sms abuse", "sms blaster", "sms aggregator abuse"], "attacks", "text message with a fake sender name",
      {"fr": "Usurpation d'identifiant d'expéditeur SMS", "sw": "Kughushi jina la mtumaji wa SMS", "rw": "Guhimba izina ry'uwohereje SMS"},
      ("A text can show any name as its sender (for example a bank or operator name) when it is sent through a bulk-SMS service, a stolen account or a fake base station, and it may even appear inside the genuine conversation thread from that sender. The name on a message proves nothing.", "Never trust a sender name or a thread: do not tap links or call numbers in such texts, check through the official app or number, and report the message to your operator. Organisations should register sender IDs and never ask for PINs by SMS."),
      ("Un SMS peut afficher n'importe quel nom d'expéditeur (par exemple celui d'une banque ou d'un opérateur) s'il passe par un service de SMS en masse, un compte volé ou une fausse antenne, et il peut même apparaître dans la vraie conversation de cet expéditeur. Le nom affiché ne prouve rien.", "Ne vous fiez jamais au nom ou au fil de discussion : ne touchez pas les liens ni les numéros de ces SMS, vérifiez via l'application ou le numéro officiel et signalez le message à votre opérateur. Les organisations doivent enregistrer leurs identifiants d'expéditeur et ne jamais demander de PIN par SMS."),
      ("SMS ishobora kwerekana izina iryo ari ryo ryose nk'uwohereje (urugero iya banki cyangwa sosiyete ya telefone) iyo inyuze kuri serivisi yohereza SMS nyinshi, konti yibwe cyangwa antene y'impimbano, ndetse ikaba yagaragara mu biganiro nyabyo by'uwo muntu. Izina riri ku butumwa nta cyo ryemeza.", "Ntukizere izina cyangwa ikiganiro: ntukande link cyangwa ngo uhamagare nimero ziri muri izo SMS, genzura unyuze kuri porogaramu cyangwa nimero yemewe, ubimenyeshe sosiyete yawe ya telefone. Ibigo bigomba kwandikisha sender IDs kandi ntibisabe PIN muri SMS."),
      ("SMS inaweza kuonyesha jina lolote kama mtumaji (mfano jina la benki au kampuni ya simu) ikipitia huduma ya SMS nyingi, akaunti iliyoibiwa au mnara bandia, na hata kuonekana ndani ya mazungumzo halisi ya mtumaji huyo. Jina kwenye ujumbe halithibitishi chochote.", "Kamwe usiamini jina la mtumaji au mazungumzo: usibofye viungo wala kupiga namba za SMS hizo, hakiki kwa programu au namba rasmi na ripoti ujumbe kwa kampuni yako ya simu. Mashirika yanapaswa kusajili vitambulisho vya mtumaji na kamwe yasiombe PIN kwa SMS.")),
    R("roaming-subscription-fraud", "Roaming fraud and subscription traps", ["roaming fraud", "subscription trap", "free trial trap", "premium subscription scam", "unwanted subscription", "vas subscription", "wap billing fraud", "airtime stealing app", "premium sms scam", "bill shock"], "attacks", "phone bill with unexpected charges",
      {"fr": "Fraude à l'itinérance et pièges d'abonnement", "sw": "Ulaghai wa roaming na mitego ya usajili", "rw": "Uburiganya bwa roaming n'imitego yo kwiyandikisha"},
      ("Fraudsters earn money from your airtime in several ways: a ‘free’ game, quiz or prize page that quietly subscribes you to a premium service, apps that send premium SMS, and abuse of roaming or premium-rate numbers. You see only mysterious deductions from your balance or bill.", "Read what a button or page subscribes you to before tapping, avoid ‘free prize’ and ‘free data’ pages, check your airtime and subscriptions regularly, unsubscribe through your operator's official code or app, and ask your operator to block premium services."),
      ("Des fraudeurs gagnent de l'argent sur votre crédit de plusieurs façons : un jeu, quiz ou page de prix « gratuit » qui vous abonne discrètement à un service premium, des applications qui envoient des SMS surtaxés, et l'abus de l'itinérance ou de numéros surtaxés. Vous ne voyez que des déductions mystérieuses sur votre solde ou facture.", "Lisez à quoi un bouton ou une page vous abonne avant de toucher, évitez les pages « prix gratuit » et « data gratuite », vérifiez régulièrement crédit et abonnements, désabonnez-vous par le code ou l'application officielle de l'opérateur et demandez-lui de bloquer les services premium."),
      ("Abariganya babona amafaranga mu mwenda wawe mu buryo bwinshi: umukino, ikibazo cyangwa urupapuro rw'igihembo «cy'ubuntu» rukwandikisha rwihishwa kuri serivisi ihenze, porogaramu zohereza SMS zihenze, no gukoresha nabi roaming cyangwa nimero zihenze. Ubona gusa amafaranga akuweho mu buryo budasobanutse.", "Soma icyo buto cyangwa urupapuro rukwandikishaho mbere yo gukanda, irinde impapuro za «igihembo cy'ubuntu» na «data y'ubuntu», genzura buri gihe amafaranga n'ibyo wiyandikishijeho, wiyandure ukoresheje code cyangwa porogaramu yemewe ya sosiyete, usabe ko ihagarika serivisi zihenze."),
      ("Matapeli hupata pesa kutoka kwa muda wako wa maongezi kwa njia nyingi: mchezo, jaribio au ukurasa wa zawadi wa ‘bure’ unaokusajili kimya kwenye huduma ya malipo, programu zinazotuma SMS za gharama na matumizi mabaya ya roaming au namba za gharama kubwa. Unaona makato ya kutatanisha tu kwenye salio au bili.", "Soma kitufe au ukurasa unakusajili kwa nini kabla ya kubonyeza, epuka kurasa za ‘zawadi ya bure’ na ‘data ya bure’, kagua salio na usajili mara kwa mara, jiondoe kwa msimbo au programu rasmi ya kampuni na uombe izuie huduma za malipo.")),
    R("gps-tracker-stalking", "AirTag and GPS tracker stalking", ["airtag stalking", "airtag", "tile tracker stalking", "gps tracker stalking", "hidden tracker", "bluetooth tracker abuse", "unwanted tracking", "tracker alert", "car tracker stalking", "find my network abuse"], "privacy", "small tracker tag hidden in a bag",
      {"fr": "Traçage par AirTag et balise GPS", "sw": "Kufuatiliwa kwa AirTag na kifuatiliaji cha GPS", "rw": "Gukurikirwa hakoreshejwe AirTag cyangwa GPS tracker"},
      ("Small Bluetooth or GPS trackers made to find lost keys can be slipped into a bag or car to follow a person without their knowledge. Phones can warn you: iPhones and Android phones alert you if an unknown tracker travels with you, and you can scan for nearby trackers.", "If you get such an alert or find a tracker, do not panic: photograph it, note where it was, check phone alerts and your belongings and vehicle, and consider contacting the police before removing or disabling it so evidence is kept. Keep phone alerts for unknown trackers turned on."),
      ("De petites balises Bluetooth ou GPS conçues pour retrouver des clés peuvent être glissées dans un sac ou une voiture pour suivre quelqu'un à son insu. Les téléphones peuvent vous prévenir : iPhone et Android alertent si une balise inconnue se déplace avec vous et vous pouvez rechercher les balises à proximité.", "Si vous recevez une alerte ou trouvez une balise, restez calme : photographiez-la, notez où elle était, vérifiez alertes, affaires et véhicule, et envisagez de contacter la police avant de l'enlever ou la désactiver pour conserver la preuve. Gardez activées les alertes de balises inconnues."),
      ("Utwuma duto twa Bluetooth cyangwa GPS tugenewe gushaka imfunguzo zataye dushobora gushyirwa mu gikapu cyangwa imodoka gukurikira umuntu atabizi. Telefone zishobora kukuburira: iPhone na Android zikumenyesha iyo tracker itazwi igendana nawe kandi ushobora gushakisha tracker ziri hafi.", "Nubona imenyesha cyangwa ukabona tracker, ntugire ubwoba: ifotore, wandike aho yari iri, genzura imenyesha, ibintu byawe n'imodoka, kandi utekereze guhamagara polisi mbere yo kuyikuraho cyangwa kuyihagarika kugira ngo ibimenyetso bibikwe. Komeza imenyesha rya tracker zitazwi rifunguye."),
      ("Vifuatiliaji vidogo vya Bluetooth au GPS vilivyotengenezwa kutafuta funguo zilizopotea vinaweza kuwekwa kwenye mfuko au gari kumfuatilia mtu bila yeye kujua. Simu zinaweza kukuonya: iPhone na Android hukutaarifu kifuatiliaji kisichojulikana kikisafiri nawe na unaweza kutafuta vifuatiliaji vilivyo karibu.", "Ukipata tahadhari au kifuatiliaji, usiogope: kipige picha, andika kilipokuwa, kagua tahadhari, mizigo na gari, na fikiria kuwasiliana na polisi kabla ya kukiondoa au kukizima ili ushahidi uhifadhiwe. Weka tahadhari za vifuatiliaji visivyojulikana zikiwa zimewashwa.")),
    R("phishing-kits-phaas", "Phishing kits and phishing-as-a-service", ["phishing kit", "phishing kits", "phishing as a service", "phaas", "phishing-as-a-service", "phishing toolkit", "ready made phishing pages", "evilginx", "modlishka", "reverse proxy phishing kit"], "social", "boxed kit of fake login pages",
      {"fr": "Kits de phishing et phishing en tant que service", "sw": "Vifaa vya phishing na phishing-as-a-service", "rw": "Phishing kits na phishing-as-a-service"},
      ("A phishing kit is a ready-made bundle of fake login pages and scripts that criminals buy or rent, often as a service (phishing-as-a-service), so people with little skill can run campaigns. Advanced kits act as a live reverse proxy that relays your real login and steals the session, defeating SMS and app codes (adversary-in-the-middle).", "Because pages can look perfect, rely on habits not looks: type the address yourself or use the official app, use passkeys or hardware keys (they refuse fake sites), report suspicious pages, and for organisations, monitor lookalike domains and request takedowns."),
      ("Un kit de phishing est un lot prêt à l'emploi de fausses pages de connexion et de scripts que les criminels achètent ou louent, souvent sous forme de service (phishing en tant que service), de sorte que des personnes peu compétentes peuvent mener des campagnes. Les kits avancés agissent comme un proxy inverse en direct qui relaie votre vraie connexion et vole la session, contournant codes SMS et applications (adversary-in-the-middle).", "Comme les pages peuvent être parfaites, fiez-vous à des habitudes, pas à l'apparence : saisissez l'adresse vous-même ou utilisez l'application officielle, utilisez passkeys ou clés matérielles (elles refusent les faux sites), signalez les pages suspectes ; pour les organisations, surveillez les domaines similaires et demandez leur retrait."),
      ("Phishing kit ni ipaki yateguwe y'impapuro z'impimbano zo kwinjira na scripts abagizi ba nabi bagura cyangwa bakodesha, akenshi nka serivisi (phishing-as-a-service), bityo abafite ubumenyi buke bashobora gukora ibikorwa. Kits zigezweho zikora nka reverse proxy ya live ikwirakwiza kwinjira kwawe nyakuri ikiba session, ikirengagiza kode za SMS na porogaramu (adversary-in-the-middle).", "Kuko impapuro zishobora gusa neza, shingira ku migirire si uko zisa: andika aderesi ubwawe cyangwa ukoreshe porogaramu yemewe, koresha passkeys cyangwa hardware keys (zanga imbuga z'impimbano), menyesha impapuro zikekwa; ku bigo, kurikirana domains zisa kandi usabe ko zikurwaho."),
      ("Phishing kit ni kifurushi kilichotayarishwa cha kurasa bandia za kuingia na skripti ambazo wahalifu hununua au kukodisha, mara nyingi kama huduma (phishing-as-a-service), hivyo watu wenye ujuzi mdogo wanaweza kuendesha kampeni. Vifaa vya hali ya juu hufanya kazi kama reverse proxy ya moja kwa moja inayopitisha kuingia kwako halisi na kuiba kikao, kukwepa misimbo ya SMS na programu (adversary-in-the-middle).", "Kwa kuwa kurasa zinaweza kuonekana kamilifu, tegemea tabia si mwonekano: andika anwani mwenyewe au tumia programu rasmi, tumia passkeys au funguo za vifaa (zinakataa tovuti bandia), ripoti kurasa za kutiliwa shaka; kwa mashirika, fuatilia vikoa vinavyofanana na uombe viondolewe.")),
    R("sms-mfa-weakness", "Weaknesses of SMS codes (and stronger multi-factor options)", ["sms mfa", "sms 2fa", "sms codes weak", "sms otp weakness", "sms two factor weakness", "why sms codes are weak", "sms code interception", "authenticator app vs sms", "mfa bypass", "mfa bypass methods", "multi factor bypass", "2fa bypass"], "identity", "phone message with a cracked lock",
      {"fr": "Faiblesses des codes SMS", "sw": "Udhaifu wa misimbo ya SMS", "rw": "Intege nke z'imibare ya SMS"},
      ("A code sent by SMS is better than no second factor, but it can be defeated: SIM swap and number porting, interception through weak telecom signalling or a fake base station, malware reading messages, and phishing pages that ask you to type the code so criminals can use it at once. MFA fatigue (spamming approval prompts) is another way around push-based MFA.", "Order of strength, generally: passkeys or hardware security keys, then authenticator-app codes (TOTP), then push approval with number matching, then SMS. Use the strongest your service offers, never read a code to anyone, and add a PIN or port-freeze with your operator."),
      ("Un code envoyé par SMS vaut mieux que pas de second facteur, mais il peut être contourné : échange de SIM et portabilité du numéro, interception via une signalisation télécom faible ou une fausse antenne, malware qui lit les messages, et pages de phishing qui vous font saisir le code pour que les criminels l'utilisent aussitôt. La fatigue MFA (spam de demandes d'approbation) contourne aussi la MFA par notification.", "Ordre de robustesse, en général : passkeys ou clés matérielles, puis codes d'application d'authentification (TOTP), puis approbation avec correspondance de numéro, puis SMS. Utilisez le plus fort proposé, ne lisez jamais un code à quelqu'un et ajoutez un code PIN ou un verrou de portabilité auprès de l'opérateur."),
      ("Kode yoherejwe muri SMS iruta kutagira urwego rwa kabiri, ariko ishobora gutsindwa: SIM swap no guhindura nimero, kuyifata binyuze ku bimenyetso bya telecom bitoroshye cyangwa antene y'impimbano, malware isoma ubutumwa, n'impapuro za phishing zigusaba kwandika kode ngo abagizi ba nabi bayikoreshe ako kanya. MFA fatigue (kohereza ibyifuzo byinshi byo kwemeza) ni ubundi buryo bwo kuyirenga.", "Uko zikomeye, muri rusange: passkeys cyangwa hardware keys, hanyuma kode za authenticator (TOTP), hanyuma kwemeza na number matching, hanyuma SMS. Koresha ikomeye serivisi yawe itanga, ntuzigere usomera umuntu kode kandi wongereho PIN cyangwa port-freeze kuri sosiyete ya telefone."),
      ("Msimbo unaotumwa kwa SMS ni bora kuliko kutokuwa na kipengele cha pili, lakini unaweza kushindwa: SIM swap na kuhamisha namba, kuingilia kupitia mawimbi dhaifu ya mawasiliano au mnara bandia, programu hasidi inayosoma ujumbe, na kurasa za hadaa zinazokuomba uandike msimbo ili wahalifu waitumie mara moja. MFA fatigue (kutuma maombi mengi ya idhini) ni njia nyingine ya kukwepa MFA ya arifa.", "Mpangilio wa nguvu, kwa ujumla: passkeys au funguo za vifaa, kisha misimbo ya programu ya authenticator (TOTP), kisha idhini yenye kulinganisha namba, kisha SMS. Tumia imara zaidi huduma inayotoa, kamwe usimsomee mtu msimbo na uongeze PIN au kufunga uhamisho wa namba kwa kampuni ya simu.")),
    R("smart-cards-piv", "Smart cards (PIV and CAC)", ["smart card", "smartcard", "piv card", "cac card", "common access card", "smart card login", "chip and pin card login", "badge authentication", "pkcs11"], "identity", "id card with a chip",
      {"fr": "Cartes à puce (PIV et CAC)", "sw": "Kadi janja (smart cards)", "rw": "Smart cards (PIV na CAC)"},
      ("A smart card is a card with a secure chip that stores a private key and certificate. You insert or tap it and enter a PIN to log in, sign documents or open doors. PIV (US federal employees) and CAC (US military) are well-known examples; the private key never leaves the chip.", "Smart cards give strong two-factor login (something you have plus a PIN) and resist phishing better than passwords. Protect the PIN, report a lost card at once so its certificate is revoked, and never lend the card."),
      ("Une carte à puce est une carte dotée d'une puce sécurisée qui stocke une clé privée et un certificat. On l'insère ou on l'approche et on saisit un PIN pour se connecter, signer des documents ou ouvrir des portes. PIV (agents fédéraux américains) et CAC (armée américaine) sont des exemples connus ; la clé privée ne quitte jamais la puce.", "Les cartes à puce donnent une double authentification forte (ce que l'on possède plus un PIN) et résistent mieux au phishing que les mots de passe. Protégez le PIN, signalez immédiatement une carte perdue pour révoquer son certificat et ne la prêtez jamais."),
      ("Smart card ni karita ifite chip irinzwe ibitse urufunguzo rwihariye na certificate. Uyishyiramo cyangwa uyiseguriraho ukandika PIN kugira ngo winjire, usinye inyandiko cyangwa ufungure inzugi. PIV (abakozi ba leta ya Amerika) na CAC (igisirikare cya Amerika) ni ingero zizwi; urufunguzo rwihariye ntirurenga chip.", "Smart cards zitanga kwinjira gukomeye kw'ibyiciro bibiri (icyo ufite hamwe na PIN) kandi zirwanya phishing kurusha amagambo y'ibanga. Rinda PIN, menyesha karita yatakaye ako kanya kugira ngo certificate yayo ikurweho kandi ntuyiguze undi."),
      ("Smart card ni kadi yenye chipu salama inayohifadhi ufunguo wa faragha na cheti. Unaiingiza au kuigusisha na kuweka PIN kuingia, kusaini hati au kufungua milango. PIV (wafanyakazi wa shirikisho la Marekani) na CAC (jeshi la Marekani) ni mifano maarufu; ufunguo wa faragha hautoki kwenye chipu.", "Smart cards hutoa kuingia kwa vipengele viwili imara (unachokimiliki pamoja na PIN) na hustahimili hadaa kuliko nywila. Linda PIN, ripoti kadi iliyopotea mara moja ili cheti chake kifutwe na kamwe usikope kadi.")),
    R("address-poisoning-dusting", "Address poisoning and dusting attacks (crypto)", ["address poisoning", "wallet address poisoning", "lookalike wallet address", "dusting attack", "crypto dusting", "dust attack", "zero value transfer scam", "transaction history copy paste scam"], "attacks", "wallet address with one swapped character",
      {"fr": "Empoisonnement d'adresse et attaque par poussière (crypto)", "sw": "Address poisoning na dusting (crypto)", "rw": "Address poisoning na dusting (crypto)"},
      ("In address poisoning a criminal sends a tiny or zero-value transaction from a wallet address that looks almost the same as one you use (same first and last characters) so it appears in your history; if you copy it from the history later you send money to the criminal. A dusting attack sends tiny amounts to many wallets to track them or lure people into phishing sites.", "Always check the full address, not just the beginning and end, use a saved address book or send a small test first, never copy addresses from transaction history, and ignore or hide unsolicited tokens instead of clicking them. Crypto transfers cannot be reversed."),
      ("Dans l'empoisonnement d'adresse, un criminel envoie une transaction minuscule ou nulle depuis une adresse presque identique à une que vous utilisez (mêmes premiers et derniers caractères) pour qu'elle apparaisse dans votre historique ; si vous la copiez plus tard depuis l'historique, vous envoyez l'argent au criminel. L'attaque par poussière envoie de minuscules montants à de nombreux portefeuilles pour les suivre ou attirer vers des sites de phishing.", "Vérifiez toujours l'adresse complète, pas seulement le début et la fin, utilisez un carnet d'adresses enregistré ou un petit envoi test, ne copiez jamais une adresse depuis l'historique et ignorez ou masquez les jetons non sollicités sans cliquer dessus. Les transferts crypto sont irréversibles."),
      ("Muri address poisoning umugizi wa nabi yohereza igikorwa gito cyane cyangwa kidafite agaciro ivuye ku aderesi isa hafi n'iyo ukoresha (inyuguti za mbere n'iza nyuma zimwe) ngo igaragare mu mateka yawe; nuyikoporora mu mateka nyuma wohereza amafaranga ku mugizi wa nabi. Dusting yohereza amafaranga make cyane kuri za wallets nyinshi kugira ngo azikurikirane cyangwa zikwegere ku mbuga za phishing.", "Genzura buri gihe aderesi yose, si intangiriro n'iherezo gusa, koresha urutonde rw'aderesi zibitse cyangwa wohereze igerageza gito, ntuzigere ukoporora aderesi mu mateka kandi wirengagize cyangwa uhishe tokens zitasabwe utazikanze. Kohereza crypto ntibisubizwa inyuma."),
      ("Katika address poisoning mhalifu hutuma muamala mdogo au wa thamani sifuri kutoka anwani inayofanana karibu na unayotumia (herufi za kwanza na za mwisho sawa) ili ionekane kwenye historia yako; ukiinakili baadaye kutoka historia unatuma pesa kwa mhalifu. Dusting hutuma kiasi kidogo kwa pochi nyingi kuzifuatilia au kuvuta watu kwenye tovuti za hadaa.", "Kagua daima anwani nzima, si mwanzo na mwisho tu, tumia kitabu cha anwani kilichohifadhiwa au tuma jaribio dogo kwanza, usinakili anwani kutoka historia na upuuze au ufiche tokeni ambazo hukuomba bila kuzibonyeza. Uhamisho wa crypto hauwezi kurejeshwa.")),
    R("sideloading-apk", "Sideloading and APK risks", ["sideloading", "side loading", "apk", "apk file", "apk risks", "install unknown apps", "unknown sources", "modded apk", "cracked apps", "third party app store", "android sideloading", "install from unknown sources", "trojanized app"], "cloud", "phone installing a file from a strange source",
      {"fr": "Chargement latéral et fichiers APK", "sw": "Sideloading na hatari za APK", "rw": "Sideloading n'ibyago bya APK"},
      ("Sideloading means installing an app from a file (an APK on Android) or from an unofficial store instead of the official one. Such files, especially ‘free’ versions of paid apps, modded games and apps sent through chat, are a leading way to deliver banking trojans, spyware and ransomware, because nobody has checked them.", "Keep ‘install unknown apps’ switched off, install from the official store, check the developer and reviews, read permissions (a flashlight does not need SMS access), keep Play Protect or the phone's scanner on, and remove apps you do not use. If you must sideload, get the file from the developer's official site and check its signature."),
      ("Le chargement latéral consiste à installer une application depuis un fichier (un APK sous Android) ou une boutique non officielle au lieu de la boutique officielle. Ces fichiers, surtout les versions « gratuites » d'applications payantes, jeux modifiés et applications reçues par messagerie, sont une voie majeure de diffusion de chevaux de Troie bancaires, logiciels espions et rançongiciels, car personne ne les a vérifiés.", "Gardez « installer des applis inconnues » désactivé, installez depuis la boutique officielle, vérifiez l'éditeur et les avis, lisez les permissions (une lampe de poche n'a pas besoin des SMS), gardez Play Protect ou l'analyse du téléphone actifs et supprimez les applis inutiles. Si vous devez charger un fichier, prenez-le sur le site officiel du développeur et vérifiez sa signature."),
      ("Sideloading ni gushyiraho porogaramu ukoresheje dosiye (APK kuri Android) cyangwa iduka ritemewe aho gukoresha iryemewe. Izo dosiye, cyane cyane verisiyo «z'ubuntu» za porogaramu zishyurwa, imikino yahinduwe na porogaramu ziza mu biganiro, ni inzira nyamukuru yo gukwirakwiza banking trojans, spyware na ransomware kuko ntawe wazigenzuye.", "Komeza «install unknown apps» ifunze, shyiraho porogaramu ziva mu iduka ryemewe, genzura uwazikoze n'ibitekerezo, soma uburenganzira (itoroshi ntikeneye SMS), usige Play Protect cyangwa scanner ya telefone ikora kandi ukureho porogaramu utakoresha. Niba ugomba sideload, fata dosiye ku rubuga rwemewe rw'uwayikoze ugenzure signature yayo."),
      ("Sideloading ni kusakinisha programu kutoka faili (APK kwenye Android) au duka lisilo rasmi badala ya duka rasmi. Faili hizo, hasa matoleo ya ‘bure’ ya programu za kulipia, michezo iliyobadilishwa na programu zinazotumwa kwenye mazungumzo, ni njia kuu ya kusambaza banking trojans, spyware na ransomware kwa sababu hakuna aliyezikagua.", "Weka ‘install unknown apps’ ikiwa imezimwa, sakinisha kutoka duka rasmi, kagua msanidi na maoni, soma ruhusa (tochi haihitaji SMS), acha Play Protect au skana ya simu ikiwa imewashwa na uondoe programu zisizotumika. Ukilazimika sideload, pata faili kwenye tovuti rasmi ya msanidi na ukague sahihi yake.")),
    R("vulnerability-prioritisation", "Vulnerability prioritisation (CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV, n-day, virtual patching)", ["vulnerability prioritisation", "vulnerability prioritization", "epss", "exploit prediction scoring system", "cisa kev", "known exploited vulnerabilities", "kev catalog", "n-day", "n-day vulnerability", "virtual patching", "exploit-db", "exploit db", "osv", "risk based patching"], "operations", "list of vulnerabilities sorted by urgency",
      {"fr": "Priorisation des vulnérabilités", "sw": "Kupa vipaumbele vya udhaifu", "rw": "Gutanga ibyihutirwa mu ntege nke"},
      ("Organisations find far more vulnerabilities than they can fix at once, so they rank them. CVSS rates technical severity; EPSS estimates the probability a flaw will be exploited soon; the CISA KEV catalogue lists flaws known to be exploited in real attacks. An n-day is a known, already-patched flaw that attackers exploit on systems not yet updated, and virtual patching blocks the exploit with a WAF/IPS rule until the real patch is installed.", "Patch first what is exploited in the wild (KEV) and exposed to the internet, then high EPSS/CVSS on critical assets. Track deadlines, keep an inventory so you know what you run, and treat virtual patching as a stopgap, not a fix."),
      ("Les organisations trouvent beaucoup plus de vulnérabilités qu'elles ne peuvent en corriger d'un coup, elles les classent donc. Le CVSS note la gravité technique ; l'EPSS estime la probabilité qu'une faille soit bientôt exploitée ; le catalogue CISA KEV recense les failles connues pour être exploitées dans de vraies attaques. Un n-day est une faille connue déjà corrigée que les attaquants exploitent sur des systèmes non mis à jour ; le patch virtuel bloque l'exploit par une règle WAF/IPS en attendant le vrai correctif.", "Corrigez d'abord ce qui est exploité dans la nature (KEV) et exposé à internet, puis les EPSS/CVSS élevés sur les actifs critiques. Suivez les échéances, tenez un inventaire pour savoir ce que vous exploitez et voyez le patch virtuel comme un palliatif, pas une solution."),
      ("Ibigo bibona intege nke nyinshi kuruta ibishobora gukosora icyarimwe, bityo birazitondeka. CVSS ipima uburemere bw'ubuhanga; EPSS ibara amahirwe y'uko intege nke zizakoreshwa vuba; urutonde CISA KEV rurimo intege nke zizwi ko zikoreshwa mu bitero nyabyo. N-day ni intege nke izwi yamaze gukosorwa abagizi ba nabi bakoresha kuri sisitemu zitaravugururwa, naho virtual patching ihagarika exploit ikoresheje ihame rya WAF/IPS kugeza ivugurura nyaryo rishyizweho.", "Banza ukosore ibikoreshwa mu bitero nyabyo (KEV) kandi biri kuri interineti, hanyuma EPSS/CVSS nyinshi ku bikoresho by'ingenzi. Kurikirana igihe ntarengwa, ugire urutonde rw'ibyo ukoresha kandi wibuke ko virtual patching ari igisubizo cy'agateganyo."),
      ("Mashirika hugundua udhaifu mwingi kuliko anavyoweza kurekebisha kwa wakati mmoja, hivyo huupa kipaumbele. CVSS hupima ukali wa kiufundi; EPSS hukadiria uwezekano wa udhaifu kutumiwa karibuni; orodha ya CISA KEV huorodhesha udhaifu unaojulikana kutumiwa kwenye mashambulizi halisi. N-day ni udhaifu unaojulikana ulioshasahihishwa ambao washambulizi hutumia kwenye mifumo isiyosasishwa, na virtual patching huzuia exploit kwa sheria ya WAF/IPS hadi kiraka halisi kisakinishwe.", "Rekebisha kwanza kinachotumiwa porini (KEV) na kilicho wazi mtandaoni, kisha EPSS/CVSS za juu kwenye mali muhimu. Fuatilia tarehe za mwisho, weka orodha ya mali ujue unachotumia na ichukulie virtual patching kama suluhisho la muda, si tiba.")),
    R("reproducible-builds", "Reproducible builds", ["reproducible builds", "reproducible build", "deterministic build", "verifiable builds", "bit for bit identical build", "build verification"], "appsec", "two machines producing identical files",
      {"fr": "Compilations reproductibles", "sw": "Reproducible builds", "rw": "Reproducible builds"},
      ("A build is reproducible when compiling the same source code, with the same tools, always produces bit-for-bit identical programs. Anyone can then rebuild the software and compare it with the published file to check that nothing was secretly added during the build.", "It defends against compromised build servers and supply-chain attacks such as SolarWinds. Projects combine it with signed releases, published checksums and software bills of materials (SBOM); users can verify checksums of downloads."),
      ("Une compilation est reproductible quand le même code source, avec les mêmes outils, produit toujours des programmes identiques bit à bit. Chacun peut alors reconstruire le logiciel et le comparer au fichier publié pour vérifier que rien n'a été ajouté en secret pendant la compilation.", "Elle protège contre les serveurs de compilation compromis et les attaques de la chaîne d'approvisionnement comme SolarWinds. Les projets l'associent à des versions signées, des empreintes publiées et des SBOM ; les utilisateurs peuvent vérifier l'empreinte des téléchargements."),
      ("Build ni reproducible iyo gukora compile code imwe y'inkomoko n'ibikoresho bimwe buri gihe bitanga porogaramu zingana bit ku bit. Buri wese ashobora kongera kubaka porogaramu akayigereranya n'iyatangajwe kugira ngo arebe ko nta kintu cyongewemo rwihishwa.", "Irinda seriveri za build zangijwe n'ibitero by'urunigi rw'itangwa nka SolarWinds. Imishinga ibihuza na releases zisinye, checksums zitangajwe na SBOM; abakoresha bashobora kugenzura checksum y'ibyo bakuyeho."),
      ("Build inaweza kuzalishwa upya wakati kuunda msimbo ule ule wa chanzo kwa zana zile zile kila mara kunatoa programu zinazofanana bit kwa bit. Kila mtu anaweza kujenga upya na kulinganisha na faili iliyochapishwa kuthibitisha hakuna kilichoongezwa kwa siri wakati wa kujenga.", "Hulinda dhidi ya seva za kujenga zilizodukuliwa na mashambulizi ya mnyororo wa ugavi kama SolarWinds. Miradi huiunganisha na matoleo yaliyosainiwa, checksums zilizochapishwa na SBOM; watumiaji wanaweza kuthibitisha checksum ya vipakuliwa.")),
    R("harvest-now-decrypt-later", "Harvest now, decrypt later and crypto-agility", ["harvest now decrypt later", "store now decrypt later", "hndl", "crypto agility", "cryptographic agility", "quantum key distribution", "qkd", "q-day", "quantum threat to encryption", "quantum safe migration", "ml-kem", "ml-dsa", "nist post-quantum standards"], "crypto", "locked box waiting for a future key",
      {"fr": "Récolter maintenant, déchiffrer plus tard et agilité cryptographique", "sw": "Harvest now, decrypt later na crypto-agility", "rw": "Harvest now, decrypt later na crypto-agility"},
      ("‘Harvest now, decrypt later’ means an adversary records encrypted traffic or stolen encrypted files today, hoping to decrypt them once powerful quantum computers can break today's public-key algorithms (RSA, elliptic curves). Crypto-agility is designing systems so algorithms can be swapped quickly. NIST published post-quantum standards in 2024 (such as ML-KEM and ML-DSA); quantum key distribution (QKD) is a different, hardware-based approach.", "Data that must stay secret for many years (health, state, long contracts) is most at risk. Inventory where public-key crypto is used, plan migration to post-quantum or hybrid schemes, use up-to-date TLS, and avoid hard-coding algorithms. Strong symmetric encryption (AES-256) is not broken by this threat."),
      ("« Récolter maintenant, déchiffrer plus tard » signifie qu'un adversaire enregistre aujourd'hui du trafic chiffré ou des fichiers chiffrés volés en espérant les déchiffrer quand des ordinateurs quantiques puissants casseront les algorithmes à clé publique actuels (RSA, courbes elliptiques). L'agilité cryptographique consiste à concevoir des systèmes dont les algorithmes se remplacent vite. Le NIST a publié en 2024 des normes post-quantiques (comme ML-KEM et ML-DSA) ; la distribution quantique de clés (QKD) est une approche matérielle différente.", "Les données qui doivent rester secrètes de longues années (santé, État, contrats longs) sont les plus exposées. Inventoriez où la cryptographie à clé publique est utilisée, planifiez la migration vers des schémas post-quantiques ou hybrides, utilisez un TLS à jour et évitez de coder les algorithmes en dur. Le chiffrement symétrique fort (AES-256) n'est pas cassé par cette menace."),
      ("«Harvest now, decrypt later» bivuze ko umwanzi abika uyu munsi amakuru afunze yafashwe cyangwa dosiye zafunzwe zibwe, yizeye kuzifungura igihe mudasobwa za quantum zikomeye zizaba zishobora kuvuna algorithms za public-key z'ubu (RSA, elliptic curves). Crypto-agility ni ugushushanya sisitemu ku buryo algorithms zisimburwa vuba. NIST yatangaje mu 2024 amahame ya post-quantum (nka ML-KEM na ML-DSA); QKD ni ubundi buryo bushingiye ku bikoresho.", "Amakuru agomba kuguma ibanga imyaka myinshi (ubuzima, leta, amasezerano maremare) ni yo ari mu kaga cyane. Andika aho public-key crypto ikoreshwa, utegure kwimukira kuri post-quantum cyangwa hybrid, koresha TLS ivuguruye kandi wirinde gushyira algorithms mu code burundu. Symmetric encryption ikomeye (AES-256) ntivunwa n'iri terabwoba."),
      ("‘Harvest now, decrypt later’ inamaanisha adui hurekodi trafiki iliyosimbwa au faili zilizoibwa leo akitumaini kuzifungua kompyuta zenye nguvu za quantum zitakapoweza kuvunja algorithms za funguo za umma za sasa (RSA, elliptic curves). Crypto-agility ni kubuni mifumo ili algorithms zibadilishwe haraka. NIST ilichapisha viwango vya post-quantum mwaka 2024 (kama ML-KEM na ML-DSA); QKD ni mbinu tofauti ya vifaa.", "Data inayopaswa kubaki siri kwa miaka mingi (afya, serikali, mikataba mirefu) iko hatarini zaidi. Orodhesha mahali crypto ya funguo za umma inatumika, panga kuhamia post-quantum au hybrid, tumia TLS iliyosasishwa na uepuke kuweka algorithms ndani ya msimbo. Usimbaji imara wa linganifu (AES-256) hauvunjwi na tishio hili.")),
    R("key-escrow-ceremony", "Key escrow and key ceremony", ["key escrow", "escrowed keys", "key recovery", "key custody", "key ceremony", "root key ceremony", "dnssec key signing ceremony", "m of n key shares", "shamir secret sharing keys", "split knowledge"], "crypto", "keys placed in a sealed vault with witnesses",
      {"fr": "Séquestre de clés et cérémonie des clés", "sw": "Key escrow na sherehe ya funguo", "rw": "Key escrow n'umuhango w'imfunguzo"},
      ("Key escrow means a trusted third party holds a copy of an encryption key so data can be recovered if the owner loses it, or accessed under legal authority; the copy becomes a target and a risk. A key ceremony is a formal, scripted and witnessed procedure for creating or using very important keys (such as a certificate authority or DNSSEC root key), often splitting the key among several people so no one holds it alone.", "Use escrow only where recovery is truly needed and protect it with strong controls and audit. For critical keys, use hardware security modules, split knowledge (m-of-n), documented steps, and test recovery, because a lost key means lost data and a stolen key means a breach."),
      ("Le séquestre de clés signifie qu'un tiers de confiance détient une copie d'une clé de chiffrement pour récupérer les données si le propriétaire la perd, ou y accéder sur autorité légale ; la copie devient une cible et un risque. Une cérémonie des clés est une procédure formelle, scénarisée et témoignée pour créer ou utiliser des clés très importantes (autorité de certification, clé racine DNSSEC), en répartissant souvent la clé entre plusieurs personnes pour que nul ne la détienne seul.", "N'utilisez le séquestre que là où la récupération est vraiment nécessaire, avec contrôles forts et audit. Pour les clés critiques, utilisez des modules matériels de sécurité (HSM), le partage de connaissance (m parmi n), des étapes documentées et testez la récupération : clé perdue = données perdues, clé volée = incident."),
      ("Key escrow bivuze ko undi muntu wizewe abika kopi y'urufunguzo rwa encryption kugira ngo amakuru agarurwe iyo nyirayo arutakaje, cyangwa ageweho n'ubuyobozi bw'amategeko; kopi iba intego n'ikibazo. Key ceremony ni uburyo bwemewe, bwanditse kandi bufite abahamya bwo gukora cyangwa gukoresha imfunguzo z'ingenzi cyane (nka certificate authority cyangwa root key ya DNSSEC), akenshi urufunguzo rugasaranganywa abantu benshi ngo ntawe uruhorana wenyine.", "Koresha escrow gusa aho kugarura bikenewe koko, ufite uburyo bukomeye n'igenzura. Ku mfunguzo z'ingenzi, koresha HSM, split knowledge (m-of-n), intambwe zanditswe kandi ugerageze kugarura: urufunguzo rwatakaye ni amakuru yatakaye, urwibwe ni igitero."),
      ("Key escrow inamaanisha mtu wa tatu anayeaminika hushikilia nakala ya ufunguo wa usimbaji ili data irejeshwe mmiliki akiupoteza, au ifikiwe kwa mamlaka ya kisheria; nakala hiyo huwa lengo na hatari. Key ceremony ni utaratibu rasmi, wa maandishi na wenye mashahidi wa kuunda au kutumia funguo muhimu sana (kama mamlaka ya vyeti au ufunguo wa mizizi wa DNSSEC), mara nyingi ufunguo hugawanywa kati ya watu kadhaa ili hakuna anayeushikilia peke yake.", "Tumia escrow pale urejeshaji unapohitajika kweli, kwa vidhibiti imara na ukaguzi. Kwa funguo muhimu, tumia HSM, maarifa yaliyogawanywa (m-kati-ya-n), hatua zilizoandikwa na ujaribu urejeshaji: ufunguo uliopotea ni data iliyopotea, ulioibiwa ni uvunjaji.")),
    R("breach-checking-combo-lists", "Checking if your data was breached (Have I Been Pwned) and combo lists", ["have i been pwned", "haveibeenpwned", "hibp", "pwned", "pwned password", "password breach", "check if my email was breached", "was my data leaked", "credential leak", "combo list", "combolist", "email password list", "leaked passwords"], "privacy", "magnifying glass over a leaked email list",
      {"fr": "Vérifier si vos données ont fuité et listes combo", "sw": "Kuangalia kama data yako ilivuja na combo lists", "rw": "Kureba niba amakuru yawe yamenetse na combo lists"},
      ("After a breach, stolen email and password pairs are bundled into combo lists that criminals feed into automated login attempts (credential stuffing). Services such as Have I Been Pwned let you check whether your email or phone number appeared in known breaches, and offer a way to check a password without sending it in full.", "Check your email addresses, and if they appear, change that password everywhere you reused it, enable MFA and watch for phishing that quotes the breach. Use a unique password per account, a password manager and breach alerts. Only use the real service's official website."),
      ("Après une fuite, les paires e-mail/mot de passe volées sont regroupées en listes combo que les criminels injectent dans des tentatives de connexion automatisées (credential stuffing). Des services comme Have I Been Pwned permettent de vérifier si votre e-mail ou numéro figure dans des fuites connues et offrent un moyen de tester un mot de passe sans l'envoyer en entier.", "Vérifiez vos adresses e-mail ; si elles apparaissent, changez ce mot de passe partout où vous l'avez réutilisé, activez la MFA et méfiez-vous du phishing qui cite la fuite. Utilisez un mot de passe unique par compte, un gestionnaire et des alertes de fuite. N'utilisez que le site officiel du vrai service."),
      ("Nyuma y'ukumeneka, imeri n'amagambo y'ibanga byibwe bikusanywa muri combo lists abagizi ba nabi bagaburira ibigeragezo byikora byo kwinjira (credential stuffing). Serivisi nka Have I Been Pwned zigufasha kureba niba imeri cyangwa nimero yawe iri mu byamenetse bizwi, kandi zitanga uburyo bwo kugenzura ijambo ry'ibanga utaryohereje ryose.", "Genzura imeri zawe; niba zigaragara, hindura iryo jambo ry'ibanga aho warikoresheje hose, fungura MFA kandi witondere phishing ivuga ukumeneka. Koresha ijambo ry'ibanga ryihariye kuri buri konti, password manager n'imenyesha ry'ukumeneka. Koresha gusa urubuga rwemewe rwa serivisi nyayo."),
      ("Baada ya uvujaji, jozi za barua pepe na nywila zilizoibwa hukusanywa kwenye combo lists ambazo wahalifu huzilisha kwenye majaribio ya kuingia ya kiotomatiki (credential stuffing). Huduma kama Have I Been Pwned hukuwezesha kuangalia kama barua pepe au namba yako ilionekana kwenye uvujaji unaojulikana, na hutoa njia ya kukagua nywila bila kuituma yote.", "Kagua anwani zako za barua pepe; zikionekana, badilisha nywila hiyo kila mahali ulipoitumia tena, washa MFA na jihadhari na hadaa inayotaja uvujaji. Tumia nywila ya kipekee kwa kila akaunti, kidhibiti cha nywila na tahadhari za uvujaji. Tumia tovuti rasmi ya huduma halisi tu.")),
    R("dark-web-monitoring-brand-protection", "Dark web monitoring and brand protection", ["dark web monitoring", "darkweb monitoring", "brand protection", "digital risk protection", "drp", "takedown service", "domain takedown", "fake social account takedown", "lookalike domain monitoring", "brand impersonation monitoring", "leaked credentials monitoring"], "operations", "radar watching for fake copies of a logo",
      {"fr": "Surveillance du dark web et protection de la marque", "sw": "Ufuatiliaji wa dark web na ulinzi wa chapa", "rw": "Gukurikirana dark web no kurinda ikirango"},
      ("Organisations watch for signs that they are being targeted: leaked staff credentials or data offered on criminal forums and leak sites, fake domains and social accounts that copy their brand to scam customers, and fraudulent apps. When found, they request takedown from registrars, hosts and platforms, and warn customers.", "For a business: monitor lookalike domains and brand mentions, set up DMARC so spoofed email is rejected, tell customers which official channels you use and never ask for PINs, and have a quick takedown and incident process. Individuals can use breach alerts for their own email."),
      ("Les organisations guettent les signes qu'elles sont visées : identifiants ou données du personnel proposés sur des forums criminels et sites de fuite, faux domaines et faux comptes sociaux qui copient leur marque pour arnaquer des clients, applications frauduleuses. Quand elles en trouvent, elles demandent le retrait aux registrars, hébergeurs et plateformes et préviennent les clients.", "Pour une entreprise : surveillez les domaines similaires et les mentions de la marque, configurez DMARC pour rejeter les e-mails usurpés, indiquez aux clients les canaux officiels et ne demandez jamais de PIN, et ayez un processus rapide de retrait et d'incident. Les particuliers peuvent utiliser des alertes de fuite pour leur e-mail."),
      ("Ibigo bikurikirana ibimenyetso by'uko bigambiriwe: amagambo y'ibanga cyangwa amakuru y'abakozi bigurishwa ku mbuga z'abagizi ba nabi n'urubuga rw'amakuru yamenetse, domains n'imbuga nkoranyambaga z'impimbano zikopera ikirango ngo ziriganye abakiriya, na porogaramu z'uburiganya. Iyo babibonye basaba abatanga domains, hosting n'imbuga kubikuraho kandi bakamenyesha abakiriya.", "Ku kigo: kurikirana domains zisa n'ibivugwa ku kirango, shyiraho DMARC ngo imeri zihimbwe zanzwe, bwira abakiriya inzira zemewe kandi ntusabe PIN, ugire uburyo bwihuse bwo gukuraho n'bwo gusubiza ibitero. Abantu ku giti cyabo bashobora gukoresha imenyesha ry'ukumeneka ku imeri zabo."),
      ("Mashirika hufuatilia dalili za kulengwa: nywila au data za wafanyakazi zinazotolewa kwenye majukwaa ya wahalifu na tovuti za uvujaji, vikoa na akaunti bandia za kijamii zinazonakili chapa kutapeli wateja, na programu za ulaghai. Zikipatikana, huomba ziondolewe kwa wasajili, wenyeji na majukwaa na kuwaonya wateja.", "Kwa biashara: fuatilia vikoa vinavyofanana na kutajwa kwa chapa, weka DMARC ili barua pepe zilizoghushiwa zikataliwe, waambie wateja njia rasmi unazotumia na kamwe usiombe PIN, na uwe na mchakato wa haraka wa kuondoa na wa matukio. Watu binafsi wanaweza kutumia tahadhari za uvujaji kwa barua pepe zao.")),
    R("reporting-phishing-scams", "How to report phishing and scams", ["report phishing", "reporting phishing", "report a phishing email", "report a scam", "report scam message", "report spam sms", "report a scam number", "how to report cybercrime", "forward phishing", "abuse report", "report suspicious message", "spam report"], "defense", "person pressing a report button",
      {"fr": "Comment signaler le phishing et les arnaques", "sw": "Jinsi ya kuripoti hadaa na utapeli", "rw": "Uko wamenyesha phishing n'uburiganya"},
      ("Reporting helps stop scams for others and helps providers block them. Report phishing e-mail with your mail app's ‘report phishing’ button, report scam texts and numbers to your mobile operator, tell the real organisation being impersonated through its official channel, and report fraud or losses to the police or the national cybercrime and cyber-security authorities of your country.", "Do not reply or click. Keep evidence (screenshots, the sender address or number, dates, payment receipts), then delete the message. If you lost money, contact your bank or mobile-money provider immediately. In Rwanda, use the official channels of the police/investigation bureau and the national cyber-security authority (NCSA) published on their official websites; never use contact details printed in the scam itself."),
      ("Signaler aide à arrêter les arnaques pour les autres et permet aux fournisseurs de les bloquer. Signalez un e-mail de phishing avec le bouton « signaler le phishing » de votre messagerie, les SMS et numéros d'arnaque à votre opérateur, informez l'organisation réellement usurpée par son canal officiel et signalez fraude ou pertes à la police ou aux autorités nationales de cybercriminalité et de cybersécurité de votre pays.", "Ne répondez pas, ne cliquez pas. Conservez les preuves (captures, adresse ou numéro de l'expéditeur, dates, reçus de paiement) puis supprimez le message. Si vous avez perdu de l'argent, contactez immédiatement votre banque ou service d'argent mobile. Au Rwanda, utilisez les canaux officiels de la police/du bureau d'enquête et de l'autorité nationale de cybersécurité (NCSA) publiés sur leurs sites officiels ; n'utilisez jamais les coordonnées figurant dans l'arnaque."),
      ("Gutanga raporo bifasha guhagarika uburiganya ku bandi no gufasha abatanga serivisi kububuza. Menyesha imeri ya phishing ukoresheje buto ya «report phishing», SMS na nimero z'uburiganya ubimenyeshe sosiyete yawe ya telefone, ubwire ikigo nyakuri cyiyitirirwa unyuze ku nzira yacyo yemewe, kandi ubuhemu cyangwa igihombo ubimenyeshe polisi cyangwa inzego z'igihugu zishinzwe cybercrime n'umutekano wa murandasi.", "Ntusubize, ntukande. Bika ibimenyetso (screenshots, aderesi cyangwa nimero y'uwohereje, amatariki, inyemezabwishyu) hanyuma usibe ubutumwa. Niba wataye amafaranga, hamagara banki cyangwa mobile money ako kanya. Mu Rwanda, koresha inzira zemewe za polisi/urwego rw'iperereza na NCSA zitangajwe ku mbuga zabo zemewe; ntuzigere ukoresha amakuru ari mu butumwa bw'uburiganya."),
      ("Kuripoti husaidia kuzuia utapeli kwa wengine na kuwezesha watoa huduma kuuzuia. Ripoti barua pepe ya hadaa kwa kitufe cha ‘report phishing’, SMS na namba za utapeli kwa kampuni yako ya simu, mwambie shirika halisi linaloigwa kupitia njia yake rasmi, na ripoti ulaghai au hasara kwa polisi au mamlaka za taifa za uhalifu wa mtandaoni na usalama wa mtandao.", "Usijibu wala kubofya. Hifadhi ushahidi (picha za skrini, anwani au namba ya mtumaji, tarehe, risiti za malipo) kisha futa ujumbe. Ukipoteza pesa, wasiliana na benki au huduma ya pesa za simu mara moja. Rwanda, tumia njia rasmi za polisi/ofisi ya upelelezi na mamlaka ya taifa ya usalama wa mtandao (NCSA) zilizochapishwa kwenye tovuti zao rasmi; kamwe usitumie mawasiliano yaliyo kwenye utapeli wenyewe.")),
    R("fake-reviews-ratings", "Fake reviews and rating manipulation", ["fake reviews", "fake review", "paid reviews", "review manipulation", "rating manipulation", "review bombing", "astroturfing", "fake testimonials", "bot reviews", "ai generated reviews", "incentivised reviews", "five star reviews fake"], "social", "row of identical five-star ratings",
      {"fr": "Faux avis et manipulation des notes", "sw": "Maoni bandia na kudanganya ukadiriaji", "rw": "Ibitekerezo by'impimbano no kugoreka amanota"},
      ("Fake reviews are positive (or negative) opinions written by paid people, bots or AI, or by the seller, to make a shop, app, product or investment look trustworthy, or to harm a competitor (review bombing). Scam shops and fake investment apps rely heavily on them.", "Be careful with many generic five-star reviews posted at once, repeated wording, reviewers with no history, and testimonials on the seller's own page. Check independent sources, look at the lowest-rated reviews, prefer ‘verified purchase’, and test with small amounts and safe payment methods before trusting a new seller."),
      ("Les faux avis sont des opinions positives (ou négatives) écrites par des personnes payées, des bots ou une IA, ou par le vendeur, pour faire paraître fiable une boutique, une application, un produit ou un placement, ou pour nuire à un concurrent (review bombing). Les fausses boutiques et fausses applis d'investissement s'y appuient beaucoup.", "Méfiez-vous de nombreux avis génériques à cinq étoiles publiés en même temps, de formulations répétées, d'auteurs sans historique et de témoignages sur la page même du vendeur. Vérifiez des sources indépendantes, lisez les avis les plus bas, préférez « achat vérifié » et testez avec de petits montants et des moyens de paiement sûrs avant de faire confiance."),
      ("Ibitekerezo by'impimbano ni ibitekerezo byiza (cyangwa bibi) byanditswe n'abishyuwe, bots cyangwa AI, cyangwa n'umucuruzi, kugira ngo iduka, porogaramu, igicuruzwa cyangwa ishoramari bisa nk'ibyizewe, cyangwa kwangiza uhanganye (review bombing). Amaduka y'uburiganya na porogaramu z'ishoramari z'impimbano zibishingiraho cyane.", "Witonde ku bitekerezo byinshi rusange by'inyenyeri eshanu byashyizweho icyarimwe, amagambo asubiramo, abanditsi nta mateka bafite n'ibyemezo biri ku rupapuro rw'umucuruzi. Genzura inkomoko zigenga, soma ibitekerezo biri hasi cyane, hitamo «verified purchase» kandi ugerageze n'amafaranga make n'uburyo bwo kwishyura butekanye mbere yo kwizera."),
      ("Maoni bandia ni maoni mazuri (au mabaya) yaliyoandikwa na watu waliolipwa, bots au AI, au muuzaji mwenyewe, ili duka, programu, bidhaa au uwekezaji uonekane unaaminika, au kumdhuru mshindani (review bombing). Maduka ya ulaghai na programu bandia za uwekezaji huyategemea sana.", "Kuwa makini na maoni mengi ya kawaida ya nyota tano yaliyochapishwa kwa wakati mmoja, maneno yanayorudiwa, waandishi wasio na historia na ushuhuda kwenye ukurasa wa muuzaji mwenyewe. Kagua vyanzo huru, soma maoni ya chini kabisa, pendelea ‘verified purchase’ na ujaribu kwa kiasi kidogo na njia salama za malipo kabla ya kuamini.")),
    R("tarpit", "Tarpit", ["tarpit", "tarpitting", "labrea", "endlessh", "slow down attackers", "tarpit honeypot", "smtp tarpit"], "network", "sticky tar slowing a runner",
      {"fr": "Tarpit (piège à ralentissement)", "sw": "Tarpit", "rw": "Tarpit"},
      ("A tarpit is a defensive trick that deliberately answers an attacker's or spammer's connections very slowly so each attempt wastes their time and resources, like a trap made of tar. Examples are tools that hold scanners on a connection for hours or delay replies to suspicious mail senders.", "Used with honeypots and mail servers to slow scanning and spam. It is an extra layer: it does not replace patching, firewalls or monitoring, and it must be set up carefully so it does not harm real users or your own capacity."),
      ("Un tarpit est une astuce défensive qui répond volontairement très lentement aux connexions d'un attaquant ou d'un spammeur pour que chaque tentative leur fasse perdre temps et ressources, comme un piège de goudron. Exemples : des outils qui retiennent des scanners des heures sur une connexion ou retardent les réponses aux expéditeurs de courrier suspects.", "Utilisé avec les honeypots et serveurs de messagerie pour ralentir scans et spam. C'est une couche supplémentaire : il ne remplace ni correctifs, ni pare-feu, ni supervision, et doit être configuré avec soin pour ne pas gêner les vrais utilisateurs ni votre capacité."),
      ("Tarpit ni amayeri y'ubwirinzi asubiza ku bushake buhoro cyane ku masano y'umushimusi cyangwa uwohereza spam, ku buryo buri kigerageza gisesagura igihe n'ibikoresho byabo, nk'umutego w'inzoka. Ingero ni ibikoresho bifata scanners ku isano amasaha cyangwa bitinza ibisubizo ku bohereza imeri bakekwa.", "Bikoreshwa hamwe na honeypots na seriveri za imeri kugabanya scanning na spam. Ni urwego rwiyongera: ntisimbura ivugurura, firewalls cyangwa gukurikirana, kandi igomba gushyirwaho neza ngo itangiza abakoresha nyabo cyangwa ubushobozi bwawe."),
      ("Tarpit ni hila ya ulinzi inayojibu kwa makusudi polepole sana miunganisho ya mshambulizi au mtumaji wa spam ili kila jaribio lipoteze muda na rasilimali zao, kama mtego wa lami. Mifano ni zana zinazoshikilia skana kwenye muunganisho kwa saa au kuchelewesha majibu kwa watumaji wa barua wanaotiliwa shaka.", "Hutumika na honeypots na seva za barua kupunguza skani na spam. Ni tabaka la ziada: haichukui nafasi ya masasisho, firewall au ufuatiliaji, na lazima iwekwe kwa uangalifu isidhuru watumiaji halisi au uwezo wako.")),
]
